TowerScout YOLO-Enabled Release Notice

Release track: agpl-yolo

TowerScout is a browser-served Flask application for identifying cooling
towers from satellite and aerial imagery. The current YOLO-enabled release
package and container image include TowerScout-authored code, third-party
Python and JavaScript dependencies, Ultralytics YOLOv5 runtime source, and
separately supplied model/data assets.

Important release statement:

Project-controlled application code, including inherited CC-marked code and
extracted modules, has the additional AGPL-3.0-only grant recorded with its
explicit path inventory in licenses/TowerScout-APPLICATION-GRANT.md.
Prior CC permissions and existing Apache grants remain available where
applicable; third-party terms and attribution remain effective.
The full YOLO-enabled package/image is not an Apache-2.0-only distribution.
Because the release includes Ultralytics YOLOv5
AGPL-3.0 code and YOLO-derived detector weights, recipients must receive the
corresponding source and license notices required for the AGPL-governed
release track.

Corresponding source for each release must include:

- TowerScout source code for the exact release ref.
- Vendored Ultralytics YOLOv5 source under webapp/vendor/yolov5_local/.
- TowerScout local YOLO patches and loader code.
- Dockerfile, Compose files, launcher scripts, packaging scripts, and import
  helpers needed to rebuild and run the release.
- Python and frontend dependency manifests.
- Build, package, asset import, and run instructions.

The release control ZIP is authoritative for release-specific source, image,
checksum, SBOM-reference, and manifest metadata. It includes SOURCE.txt with
the release source ref and source-location instructions. The package also
includes release-manifest.v1.json, IMAGE.txt, SHA256SUMS.txt, SBOM.txt,
MODEL_LICENSES.md, DATA_LICENSES.md, PROVIDER_TERMS.md, and
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The application grant and its path inventory are included
as licenses/TowerScout-APPLICATION-GRANT.md. Complete Apache-2.0, AGPL-3.0 and CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 texts are included in
licenses/, together with the bundled jQuery MIT permission notice. The container image carries compliance notices, a build-specific
SOURCE.txt and OCI labels for image/source identification.

The EfficientNet classifier weights retain the original TowerScout project's
CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 terms, including noncommercial and share-alike conditions.
Credit: TowerScout team, https://github.com/cdcai/TowerScout.
See MODEL_LICENSES.md for the exact asset identity and attribution.

TowerScout repackages U.S. Census Bureau 2025 TIGER/Line(R) ZCTA data.
TowerScout is not an original Census Bureau product. See DATA_LICENSES.md
for attribution, source and use limitations.

The source and license notices are also exposed from the local web application
at /license when the app is running.
